der children and adolescents</article-title><source>Arch Fam Med</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10728109</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wind</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>de Bourdeaudhuij</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>te Velde</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Sandvik</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Due</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Klepp</surname><given-names>KI</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><volume>38</volume><issue>4</issue><year>2006</year><fpage>211</fpage><lpage>221</lpage><article-title>Correlates of fruit and vegetable consumption among 11-year-old Belgian-Flemish and Dutch schoolchildren</article-title><source>J Nutr Educ Behav</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16785090</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zabinski</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Daly</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Norman</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Rupp</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Calfas</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Sallis</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><volume>106</volume><issue>6</issue><year>2006</year><fpage>814</fpage><lpage>821</lpage><article-title>Psychosocial correlates of fruit, vegetable, and dietary fat intake among adolescent boys and girls</article-title><source>J Am Diet Assoc</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16720122</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>de Bourdeaudhuij</surname><given-names>I</given-names><